From: Firmware Security Follow-up <security@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ext4 reject cross superblock donor early

Retain the local scoped-fd ioctl cleanup and reject a different superblock before mnt_want_write_file or ext4_move_extents can acquire locks. This is the complete upstream semantic change.

CVE: CVE-2026-74307
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c143957520c6c9b5cd72e0de8b52b814f0c576fe]

--- a/fs/ext4/ioctl.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/ioctl.c
@@ -1664,6 +1664,9 @@
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		}
 
+		if (file_inode(filp)->i_sb != file_inode(fd_file(donor))->i_sb)
+			return -EXDEV;
+
 		err = mnt_want_write_file(filp);
 		if (err)
 			return err;
